  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 202 AM EDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\n- Quiet Weather through the Weekend\n\nThe dry weather pattern continues this week under upper and \nsurface ridging. The next chance for rain is not until early next\nweek. A slowly progressive pattern sees the ridge being flattened\nby northern stream troughing early next week with a cold front \nbringing showers while slowly pushing south through the Great \nLakes.\n\n- Height falls with showers then cooler next week\n\nThere are some indications the front could stall near Lower \nMichigan with a surface low moving along it for Tuesday or\nWednesday. Upper troughing follows with the potential for sharply\ncolder temperatures for the rest of next week.",
